WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
And to explain this better, I'm going to tell you a very old joke.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
The joke is that

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Some chap, let's call him Bill. He goes to Rome for the weekend and for various kind of reasons like walking through the wrong door and kind of like happenstance.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
He's in the Vatican City, and he realizes that the Pope is dead

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
But it's Easter weekend and so kind of the authorities are keeping it quiet that the Pope is dead until after Easter Monday.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:55.000
And so he's kind of very excited about this because he's a gambling man, and so he rings his mate Ted, and he says to Ted, look, Ted, I definitely know that the Pope is dead and it's not being going to be announced until after the weekend. So you can put a bet on the Pope to die and kind of, we'll clean it, we'll make a load of money.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
And so kind of like Ted says, yeah, yeah, this is brilliant. I'll do that. I'll put this bet on

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:16.000
And so then kind of like Easter Monday comes and goes. The Pope's death is announced. Bill returns from Italy to England and he goes around Ted's house and he says, okay, you know, kind of like, you know, can I have my half of the winnings? And Ted looks really, really miserable

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:28.000
And Bill says, well, why are you looking so miserable? He said, well, you know, I got a bit carried away, and, like, I bet on the Pope and the Archbishop of Canterbury to die as an accumulator.

